# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully verified and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Nepay documentation site (Astro/Starlight project).

## What Was Found
The project already had Vercel Web Analytics properly configured:
- `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already listed in package.json
- Analytics component was already added to the custom Head component
- Dependencies just needed to be installed

## What Was Done

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
Retrieved the latest Vercel Web Analytics installation instructions from:
- https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package

### 2. Verified Framework-Specific Setup
Confirmed that for Astro projects (especially static sites using Starlight):
- The `@vercel/analytics/astro` component can be used directly
- No Vercel adapter is required for basic Analytics functionality
- The Analytics component should be imported and placed in the layout/head

### 3. Installed Dependencies
Ran `npm install` to ensure all dependencies were properly installed:
- Installed 277 packages
- @vercel/analytics v2.0.1 is now properly installed
- package-lock.json updated with current platform metadata

### 4. Verified Configuration
Confirmed the setup in `src/components/Head.astro`:
```astro
---
import Default from '@astrojs/starlight/components/Head.astro';
import Analytics from '@vercel/analytics/astro';
---

<Default><slot /></Default>
<Analytics />
```

This is the correct implementation according to Vercel's official documentation.

### 5. Tested Build
Successfully built the project:
- Build completed without errors
- 16 pages generated
- Search index built with Pagefind
- Sitemap generated

## Files Modified
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with installed dependencies

## Configuration Details
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1
- **Framework**: Astro v7.4.4 with Starlight v0.42.7
- **Integration**: Analytics component added to custom Head.astro component
- **Build**: Static site generation (no adapter required)

## Deployment Notes
Once deployed to Vercel, the Analytics will automatically start tracking:
- Page views
- Visitor metrics
- Performance data

The Analytics component works in production mode by default and will collect data when the site is deployed on Vercel's platform.

## Testing
✅ Dependencies installed successfully
✅ Build completes without errors
✅ Analytics component properly imported and configured
✅ No linter or test errors (no scripts configured)

The implementation follows Vercel's official documentation and best practices for Astro projects.
